257
00:14:25,793 --> 00:14:29,510
Well, I need you to give it back to
me, so fork it over now, Mondatta!

258
00:14:29,593 --> 00:14:30,593
Right, let's see.

259
00:14:31,733 --> 00:14:32,563
Crap!

260
00:14:32,646 --> 00:14:34,137
We've only got 40 seconds left!

261
00:14:34,233 --> 00:14:35,433
Move your ass!

262
00:14:36,793 --> 00:14:37,623
Uh...

263
00:14:37,706 --> 00:14:40,664
I-I don't know if this is
enough, but go ahead and take it!

264
00:14:40,833 --> 00:14:41,663
Ah!

265
00:14:42,233 --> 00:14:43,063
Whooo!

266
00:14:44,693 --> 00:14:47,869
Hey, I think I saw one of
them roll behind the bricks.

267
00:14:48,513 --> 00:14:51,190
They're just coins, but
there are a lot of them.

268
00:14:51,273 --> 00:14:52,103
Nice.

269
00:14:52,186 --> 00:14:53,793
Must be at least 20 pounds.

270
00:14:54,053 --> 00:14:55,090
Hey, man, watch your feet.

271
00:14:55,173 --> 00:14:56,003
You're steppin' on one.

272
00:14:56,086 --> 00:14:56,916
What's that?

273
00:14:56,999 --> 00:14:57,829
Ah!

274
00:14:57,912 --> 00:14:58,950
Pick up the damn coins later!

275
00:14:59,033 --> 00:15:00,630
You can have them all, okay?

276
00:15:00,713 --> 00:15:02,213
Here you go, boys.

277
00:15:02,533 --> 00:15:04,121
It's getting close to noon.

278
00:15:04,313 --> 00:15:08,193
I made you boys some tea, so take
a load off and have some lunch.

279
00:15:08,493 --> 00:15:10,113
Oh, sounds good to me.

280
00:15:10,233 --> 00:15:13,133
Listen, Granny, I found
them first, so get lost!

281
00:15:13,413 --> 00:15:15,060
Thank you very much, ma 'am.

282
00:15:16,893 --> 00:15:17,993
Put them down!

283
00:15:18,273 --> 00:15:20,230
I told you to hurry up and open the pipe!

284
00:15:20,313 --> 00:15:22,489
If you don't, I'll crack your skulls!

285
00:15:29,393 --> 00:15:30,413
It's open!

286
00:15:30,733 --> 00:15:31,633
Move it!

287
00:15:34,473 --> 00:15:36,393
Now die, Jotaro!

288
00:15:39,493 --> 00:15:40,553
I won!

289
00:15:40,873 --> 00:15:44,790
Just like the predictions said, I shot
the cocky bastard at the stroke of noon!

290
00:15:44,873 --> 00:15:45,893
Go get him!

291
00:15:54,053 --> 00:15:55,953
Old man, time to get up.

292
00:16:00,133 --> 00:16:02,662
I don't think there's
any permanent damage.

293
00:16:03,333 --> 00:16:05,413
I only have cuts and bruises.

294
00:16:05,833 --> 00:16:08,333
But Polnareff, on the other hand...

295
00:16:09,793 --> 00:16:12,390
Hey, don't mean to be a nuisance, but...

296
00:16:12,473 --> 00:16:15,061
Could someone get this
damn thing off of me?

297
00:16:19,313 --> 00:16:20,333
I won!

298
00:16:20,713 --> 00:16:22,360
This is really gonna happen!

299
00:16:22,613 --> 00:16:24,789
Tojoro's right in front of that pipe!

300
00:16:34,513 --> 00:16:36,253
Huh? Ah, shoot!

301
00:16:41,793 --> 00:16:42,623
What?!

302
00:16:45,893 --> 00:16:46,723
Watch it.

303
00:16:48,073 --> 00:16:49,544
Sorry about that, Jotaro.

304
00:16:49,893 --> 00:16:51,830
I don't know what Whole
Horse was thinking!

305
00:16:51,913 --> 00:16:53,770
But he decided sticking
his fingers on my nose?

306
00:16:53,853 --> 00:16:55,850
would be the perfect way
to spend the evening.

307
00:16:55,933 --> 00:16:57,853
That guy is très disgusting.

308
00:16:58,393 --> 00:17:00,013
And my nose still itches.

309
00:17:00,373 --> 00:17:01,673
So sorry again.

310
00:17:02,193 --> 00:17:04,013
But how's it possible?

311
00:17:04,513 --> 00:17:06,293
My bullet's missed!

312
00:17:08,073 --> 00:17:09,813
What the hell?

313
00:17:10,153 --> 00:17:12,230
Were you trying to pull one over on me?

314
00:17:12,313 --> 00:17:14,330
What the hell is going on around here?

315
00:17:14,413 --> 00:17:16,053
I have no idea, yes.

316
00:17:16,233 --> 00:17:20,293
Like I said, my predictions
always come true. It's fate.

317
00:17:20,473 --> 00:17:21,613
I can't believe it.

318
00:17:21,813 --> 00:17:26,070
Not once since I started using my stand
have my predictions ever been wrong.

319
00:17:26,153 --> 00:17:29,650
Well, clearly there's a first time for
everything because they're still alive.

320
00:17:29,733 --> 00:17:31,550
Not a single bullet hit his mark.

321
00:17:31,633 --> 00:17:34,633
It's safe to say your
prediction was totally wrong.

322
00:17:34,973 --> 00:17:35,803
Damn you.

323
00:17:36,833 --> 00:17:39,270
Thanks for joining us
for today's broadcast.

324
00:17:39,353 --> 00:17:40,790
Be sure to tune in next time.

325
00:17:40,873 --> 00:17:42,579
Now for the 12 o 'clock news.

326
00:17:44,413 --> 00:17:45,243
Huh?

327
00:17:48,013 --> 00:17:49,073
What the hell?

328
00:17:50,053 --> 00:17:52,582
There's no way in hell
it's just now, Noon.

329
00:17:53,993 --> 00:17:55,373
I know what happened.

330
00:17:56,193 --> 00:17:57,953
My watch is...

331
00:17:59,213 --> 00:18:00,973
My watch is fast.

332
00:18:01,713 --> 00:18:05,853
And that means I ended up firing
off the bullets before it was time.

333
00:18:06,093 --> 00:18:07,453
But now it is, Noon.

334
00:18:07,793 --> 00:18:09,270
What's that mean for us, huh?

335
00:18:09,353 --> 00:18:14,013
Tell me, what the hell's going to happen
to us now that we've gone off script?

336
00:18:15,533 --> 00:18:17,153
No, it can't be.

337
00:18:22,793 --> 00:18:24,490
But where do we get off track?

338
00:18:24,573 --> 00:18:26,090
It said the bullets will go right through

339
00:18:26,173 --> 00:18:28,530
Joe Tarot's forehead
at the stroke of noon.

340
00:18:28,613 --> 00:18:30,010
Hall Horse, the bullets are...

341
00:18:30,093 --> 00:18:30,923
Come on!

342
00:18:31,053 --> 00:18:33,994
All I need to know is
what's going to happen next!

343
00:18:44,673 --> 00:18:48,732
Hey, tell me I'm not the only one
who heard that ear-piercing scream.

344
00:18:49,033 --> 00:18:52,590
I'm not clear on the details, but
there's something fishy going on here.

345
00:18:52,673 --> 00:18:54,730
But the bigger concern is this truck.

346
00:18:54,813 --> 00:18:58,050
I think we'd better get out of here
before the cops start showing up.

347
00:18:58,133 --> 00:18:59,074
Let's move, man.

348
00:18:59,253 --> 00:19:03,733
But before we go, I want to know where
Whole Horse ran off to. I don't know.

349
00:19:03,953 --> 00:19:05,777
He disappeared for some reason.

350
00:19:12,573 --> 00:19:16,210
Hey, if you don't get away from that
pipe, you're going to get soaking wet.

351
00:19:16,293 --> 00:19:18,293
You should try to be more careful.

352
00:19:24,993 --> 00:19:25,833
Is he dead?

353
00:19:26,233 --> 00:19:27,653
No, but he's critical.

354
00:19:28,613 --> 00:19:32,201
I couldn't even begin to tell
you what transpired here today.

355
00:19:32,453 --> 00:19:34,830
They looked him over and it
seems as though the bullet

356
00:19:34,913 --> 00:19:37,210
went through his forehead
and out the top of his head.

357
00:19:37,293 --> 00:19:40,290
One centimeter lower, and
he would have been a goner.

358
00:19:40,373 --> 00:19:41,203
Oof.

359
00:19:41,286 --> 00:19:43,613
Gotta say, that is one lucky man.

360
00:19:48,253 --> 00:19:50,993
In the end, it seems my
prediction was right.

361
00:19:51,693 --> 00:19:55,273
Which means this was Whole
Horse's fate all along.

362
00:19:56,413 --> 00:19:58,273
Jojo is really something else.

363
00:19:58,633 --> 00:20:00,653
How lucky can one person be?

364
00:20:01,133 --> 00:20:04,430
Both my brother and Whole
Horse were defeated by fate.

365
00:20:04,513 --> 00:20:07,613
At this point, we stand
users are wasting our time.

366
00:20:07,813 --> 00:20:10,460
Master Days, the only
one who can defeat him.

367
00:20:12,353 --> 00:20:13,893
You know what, Zenyatta?

368
00:20:14,433 --> 00:20:17,033
Whole Horse, that big buffoon of a man,

369
00:20:17,293 --> 00:20:20,764
taught me that revenge is
nothing more than a massive joke.

370
00:20:21,133 --> 00:20:23,733
So, I'm going to forget about Jotaro.

371
00:20:24,353 --> 00:20:26,093
I have a new path in life.

372
00:20:26,313 --> 00:20:29,933
I'll use my stand's powers to
help as many people as I can.

373
00:20:30,193 --> 00:20:32,840
I'll use them to bring
happiness to everyone.

374
00:20:33,513 --> 00:20:35,572
Maybe people will start to like us.

375
00:20:35,673 --> 00:20:38,202
And just maybe our
future will be brighter.

376
00:20:43,413 --> 00:20:44,953
I'm tired of being afraid.

377
00:20:45,193 --> 00:20:48,730
Today's the last day I spend under
a box cowering from everyone.

378
00:20:48,813 --> 00:20:50,710
I learned a lot from this battle.

379
00:20:50,793 --> 00:20:52,350
More than I thought I could.

380
00:20:52,433 --> 00:20:54,139
I'm coming home now, brother.

381
00:20:54,413 --> 00:20:56,933
I'm coming home to ask one to join you.

382
00:20:59,733 --> 00:21:00,563
Huh? Huh?

383
00:21:00,853 --> 00:21:02,933
Oh my gosh, I am so sorry.

384
00:21:03,053 --> 00:21:04,759
I kicked it without thinking.

385
00:21:05,613 --> 00:21:06,610
I didn't mean to hit you.

386
00:21:06,693 --> 00:21:09,073
Please forgive me. Hold on.

387
00:21:09,313 --> 00:21:11,713
This dog, he looks familiar.

388
00:21:12,033 --> 00:21:14,209
I'm pretty sure I've seen him before.

389
00:21:14,413 --> 00:21:15,453
But where?

390
00:21:17,033 --> 00:21:17,863
Ah!

391
00:21:17,993 --> 00:21:19,353
There's no way!

392
00:21:19,733 --> 00:21:20,653
It can't be!

393
00:21:21,733 --> 00:21:22,563
No!

394
00:21:27,073 --> 00:21:30,490
Hey, now that I think about
it, where'd our dumbass dog go?

395
00:21:30,573 --> 00:21:31,970
You're talking about Iggy?

396
00:21:32,053 --> 00:21:34,710
I'm sure he's scrounging
around for food somewhere.

397
00:21:34,793 --> 00:21:38,590
I've said from the beginning he
wouldn't help us when we needed him.

398
00:21:38,673 --> 00:21:41,370
He should have known it
wouldn't be so simple.

399
00:21:41,453 --> 00:21:45,041
If people could change that
easily, life wouldn't be so hard.

400
00:21:46,053 --> 00:21:49,730
So as fate would have it, Mondatta
joined Whole Horse in the hospital.

401
00:21:49,813 --> 00:21:52,953
Only now, he was meager than ever before.

402
00:21:53,933 --> 00:21:54,813
But, um...

403
00:21:56,133 --> 00:21:59,893
Do you believe it?

404
00:22:00,793 --> 00:22:01,673
I believe it!

405
00:22:02,433 --> 00:22:04,833
Hell Horse! Bang! Compa!

406
00:22:05,973 --> 00:22:07,914
I'm the player of the Hall Horse.

407
00:22:11,893 --> 00:22:14,890
The card's name is Emperor.

408
00:22:14,973 --> 00:22:17,233
I'm going to fight with the two-man.

409
00:22:18,493 --> 00:22:21,273
I'm going to fight with someone.

410
00:22:21,973 --> 00:22:23,953
But you're okay with this?

411
00:22:25,733 --> 00:22:34,253
I'm a Boingo man.

412
00:22:35,093 --> 00:22:39,270
I'm a Bang

413
00:22:39,353 --> 00:22:42,290
-go man.

414
00:22:42,373 --> 00:22:44,093
It's 100 %!

415
00:22:45,593 --> 00:22:46,510
It's 100 %!

416
00:22:46,593 --> 00:22:48,550
But this is how it's going to work?

417
00:22:48,633 --> 00:22:51,751
I don't have to believe it's
going to be a good idea.

418
00:22:52,353 --> 00:22:56,093
The fact that you're going to
print out is the best thing.

419
00:22:56,873 --> 00:22:58,049
It's the best thing.

420
00:22:58,773 --> 00:23:00,250
The fact that you're going
to be the best thing.

421
00:23:00,333 --> 00:23:03,733
If you're going to do it,

422
00:23:04,853 --> 00:23:06,473
it's all going to work.

423
00:23:06,953 --> 00:23:08,350
You're going to believe it.

424
00:23:08,433 --> 00:23:09,263
First!

425
00:23:09,346 --> 00:23:10,993
Hot Horse, Boingo, Combi!

426
00:23:11,813 --> 00:23:13,433
I believe, yes!

427
00:23:13,793 --> 00:23:14,793
OK, I believe!

428
00:23:15,413 --> 00:23:17,693
Hot Horse, Boingo, Combi!

429
00:23:18,513 --> 00:23:22,533
The truth is that I can't read correctly!

430
00:23:39,153 --> 00:23:41,388
I have a soft spot for kid dog lovers.
